      "documentConcept": "Alpha-synuclein seed amplification assay and fluid biomarkers",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:dc396c309c1d0039197f646a0cf2a6622e52d1f7e44d084ae064d7242a8e0008",
      "text": "Alpha-synuclein seed amplification assays amplify seeding-competent aggregates and provide a molecular biomarker of synuclein pathology. CSF studies show strong diagnostic performance in selected cohorts, with clinically important heterogeneity in sensitivity. Cross-laboratory results are encouraging, but protocol and preanalytical standardization remain necessary. Diagnostic positivity is distinct from validated measurement of severity or progression. Blood assays offer less invasive sampling while introducing contamination and handling challenges. Neurofilament light chain measures neuroaxonal injury and can complement SAA, with interpretation influenced by biological covariates. FDA support described here concerns trial enrichment in its 2024 letter. Skin biopsy detection of phosphorylated alpha-synuclein is another tissue biomarker under evaluation.",
